nly the reading/research phase was completed before interruption.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified a minor conflict: D2 says \"Use the standard flag package\" but the reference code (cmd/mv/main.go) uses manual flag parsing. The pattern from other cmd/ packages should be followed (manual parsing).\n   - Identified all flags from srd058-rm that need to be declared: -r, -R, --recursive, -f, --force, -d, --dir, -i, -I, -v, --verbose, --interactive=WHEN (never/once/always)\n   - Identified the interactive mode enum values needed: never (like -f), once (like -I), always (like -i)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single user message is the massive stitch task prompt containing: role definition, repository_files list, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, the task description itself (with required_reading, files, requirements, design_decisions, acceptance_criteria), shared_protocols, package_contracts, and constraints.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/rm/main.go` with:\n     - Copyright header\n     - Package doc comment referencing srd058-rm\n     - All imports\n     - Interactive mode type enum (never/once/always)\n     - Options struct with all flag fields (recursive, force, dir, interactiveMode, verbose)\n     - `func main()` calling `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, `parseFlags`, and stub dispatch\n     - `parseFlags` function handling all short and long flags\n     - Stub function signatures for: `removeFiles`, `removeFile`, `removeDir`, `promptRemoval`, `isDotOrDotDot`, etc.\n     - Each stub should compile but print \"not implemented\" and os.Exit(1) per D3\n   - Create `cmd/rm/rm_test.go` with:\n     - Copyright header\n     - TestDiff using `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"grm\")`\n     - `t.Skip` if grm not found\n     - Empty `tests` slice\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/rm ./cmd/rm/`, `go vet ./cmd/rm/`, `go test